{"slug": "hide-the-delete-button-on-the-screen", "title": "Clarity PPM Technical Tip: How to hide “Delete” button using UI Themes", "category": "Configuration", "categorySlug": "configuration", "date": "Nov 25, 2019", "author": "admin", "image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262861/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/letter2.webp", "excerpt": "How often have you wanted a separate Delete rights similar to Create rights in Clarity PPM?", "readTime": 3, "content": "<ul class=\"post-info\">\n                                            <li style=\"list-style:none;padding-bottom:0\"></li>\n                                            <li style=\"list-style:none;padding-bottom:0\"></li>\n                                        </ul>\n                                    </div> -->\n                                    \n<p><b>Problem Scenario:</b></p>\n<p>In PPM, most of the edit and delete security right over objects are coupled together. Meaning if a user has the rights to edit/create an object instance, they also inherit the rights to delete the object instance. There is no way to restrict the user not to delete the object instances. The below solution, helps in hiding the &#8216;Delete&#8217; button with the help of the UI themes hence preventing the deletion. This solution is SaaS compliant and does not involve writing any triggers on the database.</p>\n<p><b>Solution:</b></p>\n<p>1. Right Click on the &#8216;Delete&#8217; button that needs to hidden, and click on &#8216;Inspect&#8217;.</p>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1704 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262858/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"1473\" height=\"1208\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262858/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect.webp 1473w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262855/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect-300x246.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262853/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect-1024x840.webp 1024w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262857/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect-768x630.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262856/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect-67x55.webp 67w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262854/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_inspect-200x164.webp 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1473px) 100vw, 1473px\" /></p>\n<p>2. Obtain the button navigation code from the inspect window. It should be similar to below &#8211;<br />\n<img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1705 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262846/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"1152\" height=\"332\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262846/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code.webp 1152w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262844/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code-300x86.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262840/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code-1024x295.webp 1024w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262845/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code-768x221.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262842/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code-175x50.webp 175w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262842/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_code-200x58.webp 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1152px) 100vw, 1152px\" /></p>\n<p>3. The following condition using the button unique identifier can be added to the end of the UI theme which will hide the button in context.</p>\n<p><b><em style=\"font-style: italic; color: black;\">button[onclick*=&#8221;&#8216;itl.riskDeleteConfirm'&#8221;]{display: none;}</em></b></p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1706 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262852/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"1358\" height=\"650\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262852/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden.webp 1358w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262850/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden-300x144.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262847/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden-1024x490.webp 1024w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262851/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden-768x368.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262848/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden-115x55.webp 115w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262849/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/11/Delete_button_hidden-200x96.webp 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1358px) 100vw, 1358px\" /></p>\n<p>4. The above added line can be removed to make the &#8216;Delete&#8217; button visible again.</p>\n<p><b>Author:</b> Gangadhar, PPM Consultant<br />\n<b>Contact us:</b><br />\nFor any questions or have enquiries about our PPM service offerings please contact us at <a href=\"mailto:info@albatrozsolutions.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">info@albatrozsolutions.com</a> or <a href=\"mailto:balaji@albatrozsolutions.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">balaji@albatrozsolutions.com</a>. We will be glad to help.</p>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                            \n                            <div class=\"col-md-12\">\n                                <a href=\"https://albatrozsolutions.com/contact-us/\" style=\"margin-top: 15px;text-align:center;width: aut